        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6d73ae18-d2c6-552d-8e9f-576aac2ea30b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Castres, Languedoc, France, Italy\n- Buildings: Castres Cathedral, Saint Benoît church\n- People: Benedict of Nursia, Scholastica\n- Organizations: Eastern Orthodox Churches, Catholic Church, Oriental Orthodox Churches, Anglican Communion, Old Catholic Churches\n- Concepts: Christian saints, patron saints of Europe\n\nFacts:\n- Benedict of Nursia was born on 2 March 480 and died in 543 or 547 AD.\n- Benedict of Nursia was a Christian saint venerated in the Eastern Orthodox Churches, the Catholic Church, the Oriental Orthodox Churches, the Anglican Communion, and the Old Catholic Churches.\n- Benedict of Nursia is a patron saint of Europe.\n- According to a ninth-century tradition, Scholastica was born in Italy and was the twin sister of Benedict of Nursia.\n- Castres Cathedral, also called Cathédrale Saint-Benoît de Castres, is now the Roman Catholic church of Saint Benoît in Castres, Languedoc, France.\n- Castres Cathedral is a historical religious building.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
